2,GPIO_TC_002,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,gpio_reg_wr_rd_test,"Verify write and read-back of all writable GPIO registers using multiple data patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000). Write each pattern to all writable registers and read back to verify.",Register Write/Read Verification,GPIO,"gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10, gp0_gpio_11, gp0_gpio_12, gp0_gpio_13, gp0_gpio_14, gp0_gpio_15, gp0_gpio_16, gp0_gpio_17, gp0_gpio_18, gp0_gpio_19, gp0_gpio_20, gp0_gpio_21, gp0_gpio_22, gp0_gpio_23, gp0_gpio_24, gp0_gpio_25, gp0_gpio_26, gp0_gpio_27, gp0_gpio_28, gp0_gpio_29, gp0_gpio_30, gp0_gpio_31, gp0_gpio_32, gp0_gpio_33, gp0_gpio_34, gp0_gpio_35, gp0_gpio_36, gp0_gpio_37, gp0_gpio_38, gp0_gpio_39, gpio_intr_raw_stclr1, gp0_intr1_intr_en1, gp0_intr1_intr_sts1, gp0_intr2_intr_en1, gp0_intr2_intr_sts1, gpio_io_ctrl_group1, gpio_io_ctrl_group2, gpio_io_ctrl_group3, gpio_io_ctrl_group4, gpio_dout_group1, gpio_dout_group2, gpio_dout_group3, gpio_dout_group4, gpio_din_group1, gpio_din_group2, gpio_din_group3, gpio_din_group4","pedge_intr_en, nedge_intr_en, level_sel, io_ctrl, dout, G8-G39_intr_en, G8-G39_io_ctrl, G8-G39_io_wr_mask, G8-G39_dout, G8-G39_dout_wr_mask","0x00-0x7C (per-GPIO), 0x80, 0x84, 0x88, 0x8C, 0x90, 0x94, 0x98, 0x9C, 0xA0, 0xA4, 0xA8, 0xAC, 0xB0, 0xB4, 0xB8, 0xBC, 0xC0","RW, RW2, VRRW","io_ctrl=1, all others=0",Per register write_mask from spec,Per register read_mask from spec,"1. For each data pattern in {0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000}:
  a. Write (pattern & write_mask) to each writable register.
  b. Skip RO registers and registers in skip_array.
  c. Read back each register.
  d. Compute expected = (pattern & read_mask & write_mask) | (~write_mask & read_mask & default_value).
  e. Compare read value with expected.
2. Report PASS/FAIL per register per pattern.","Read-back value must match expected value computed from write_mask, read_mask, and default values for all 6 data patterns across all writable registers.",PASS if wr_fail_cnt == 0 for all patterns; FAIL if any write-read mismatch detected.,gp0_autoreg.xlsx - RegSpec sheet (Rows 9-584),Covered,Skips VRRW registers (skip_array[32]=1 for gpio_intr_raw_stclr1 and skip_array[37-48]=1 for group registers). RO registers (data_in/intr_raw_sts/intr_sts) are skipped for write. WO register (intr_clr) skipped for read-back.
3,GPIO_TC_003,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"Verify GPIO level-sensitive interrupt generation for active HIGH level. Configure each GPIO pin (8-39) in input mode with level_sel=1 (active high), enable group interrupt, drive input high, and verify interrupt is raised and can be cleared.",Interrupt - Active High Level,GPIO,"gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39, gp0_intr1_intr_en1, gp0_intr1_intr_sts1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1","io_ctrl (bit 20), level_sel (bit 19), intr_raw_sts (bit 1), intr_clr (bit 16), G8-G39_intr_en, G8-G39_intr_sts, gpio0_intr/gpio1_intr","0x00-0x7C (per-GPIO), 0x84, 0x88, LSS SYSREG offsets 0x28, 0x24","RW, RW2, RO, WO, VRRW","io_ctrl=1, level_sel=0, intr_raw_sts=0",NA,NA,"1. Enable GIC IRQ (87 for GPIO0 / 88 for GPIO1).
2. Enable sysreg interrupt (write LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1).
3. For each GPIO pin i (0 to 31):
  a. Write 0x00180000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) → sets io_ctrl=1 (input mode), level_sel=1 (active high).
  b. Write (1<<i) to gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (0x84) to enable group interrupt for pin i.
  c. Drive GPIO input high (write 0xFFFFFFFF to SRAM 0xA0243FFC).
  d. Wait for interrupt (int_pend loop).
4. In ISR (Default_IRQHandler):
  a. Read gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) and check intr_raw_sts (bit 1) is set.
  b. Read gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (0x88) and verify bit i is set.
  c. Clear interrupt by writing 0x00110000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) (intr_clr=1).
  d. Read back and verify interrupt cleared (expected 0x100001).
  e. Disable group interrupt (write 0x0 to 0x84).
  f. Verify group interrupt status cleared.
  g. Clear sysreg interrupt status.","For each GPIO pin: intr_raw_sts bit must be set when input is high with level_sel=1. Group interrupt status bit must be set. After clearing, intr_raw_sts must be 0 and group status must be 0. Sysreg status must clear successfully.",PASS if test_err == 0 (all 32 pins pass interrupt raise and clear); FAIL if any pin fails interrupt detection or clearing.,"gp0_autoreg.xlsx - RegSpec (gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39: level_sel bit 19, io_ctrl bit 20, intr_raw_sts bit 1, intr_clr bit 16); gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (0x84); gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (0x88); LSS_REGS PDF (raw_stcr1 offset 0x24: gpio0_intr bit 1, gpio1_intr bit 2; intr_en1 offset 0x28)",Covered,Uses #ifdef GPIO0 / GPIO1 conditional compilation. Tests all 32 GPIO pins (8-39) sequentially. Validates both interrupt assertion and clearing.
4,GPIO_TC_004,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en,"Verify GPIO level-sensitive interrupt generation for active LOW level. Configure each GPIO pin (8-39) in input mode with level_sel=0 (active low), enable group interrupt, drive input low, and verify interrupt is raised and can be cleared.",Interrupt - Active Low Level,GPIO,"gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39, gp0_intr1_intr_en1, gp0_intr1_intr_sts1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1","io_ctrl (bit 20), level_sel (bit 19), intr_raw_sts (bit 1), intr_clr (bit 16), G8-G39_intr_en, G8-G39_intr_sts, gpio0_intr/gpio1_intr","0x00-0x7C (per-GPIO), 0x84, 0x88, LSS SYSREG offsets 0x28, 0x24","RW, RW2, RO, WO, VRRW","io_ctrl=1, level_sel=0, intr_raw_sts=0",NA,NA,"1. Enable GIC IRQ (87 for GPIO0 / 88 for GPIO1).
2. Enable sysreg interrupt (write LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1).
3. For each GPIO pin i (0 to 31):
  a. Write 0x00100000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) → sets io_ctrl=1 (input mode), level_sel=0 (active low).
  b. Write (1<<i) to gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (0x84) to enable group interrupt for pin i.
  c. Drive GPIO input low (write ~(1<<i) to SRAM 0xA0243FFC).
  d. Wait for interrupt (int_pend loop).
4. In ISR (Default_IRQHandler):
  a. Read gp0_gpio_8+(i*4) and check intr_raw_sts (bit 1) is set.
  b. Read gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (0x88) and verify bit i is set.
  c. Clear interrupt by writing 0x00110000 to gp0_gpio_8+(i*4).
  d. Read back and verify interrupt cleared.
  e. Disable group interrupt and verify status cleared.
  f. Clear sysreg interrupt status.","For each GPIO pin: intr_raw_sts bit must be set when input is low with level_sel=0. Group interrupt status bit must be set. After clearing, all interrupt status bits must be 0.",PASS if test_err == 0 (all 32 pins pass interrupt raise and clear for active low); FAIL if any pin fails.,"gp0_autoreg.xlsx - RegSpec (gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39: level_sel bit 19, io_ctrl bit 20, intr_raw_sts bit 1, intr_clr bit 16); gp0_intr1_intr_en1 (0x84); gp0_intr1_intr_sts1 (0x88); LSS_REGS PDF (raw_stcr1 offset 0x24: gpio0_intr bit 1, gpio1_intr bit 2; intr_en1 offset 0x28)",Covered,Active low level selection test. Same ISR handler as TC_003. Tests all 32 GPIO pins sequentially with inverted input pattern.
